%N A398138 Sum of the remainders k mod n over the distinct entries k of the n X n multiplication table.
%C A398138 This is a positive-indexed distinct-product analog of the remainder distribution A095026, which counts ordered factor pairs in the zero-based n X n multiplication table.
%H A398138 Frédéric D. W. Heidenthal-König, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19102497">The Support of the Euclidean Decomposition of the Multiplication Table</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A398138 Frédéric D. W. Heidenthal-König, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19273836">Euclidean Transport of Multiplication</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%F A398138 a(n) = Sum_{k in {i*j: 1 <= i, j <= n}} (k mod n).
%F A398138 a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n^2} (k mod n) * A394016(n,k).
%F A398138 a(n) = A321165(n) - n * A397038(n).
%e A398138 The distinct entries of the 3 X 3 multiplication table are 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 9. Their remainders modulo 3 are 1, 2, 0, 1, 0, 0, so a(3) = 4.
%o A398138 (Python)
%o A398138 def a(n):
%o A398138     products = set()
%o A398138     for i in range(1, n + 1):
%o A398138         for j in range(1, n + 1):
%o A398138             products.add(i * j)
%o A398138     return sum(k % n for k in products)
%o A398138 n = 50
%o A398138 print([a(k) for k in range(1, n + 1)])
%o A398138 (PARI) a(n) = vecsum(apply(x->x%n, setbinop((x,y)->x*y, [1..n]))); \\ _Michel Marcus_, Jul 21 2026
%Y A398138 Cf. A027424, A095026, A321165, A394016, A397038.
%K A398138 nonn,new
